  "recipeCuisine": "Japan",
  "name": "Agedashi Dofu",
  "text": "Agedashi Dofu\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time: 10 minutes\n\nYield: 2\n\nIngredients\n\n200g firm tofu,\n\nGrated white radish (daikon)\n\nSpring onions, chopped\n\nBonito Flakes\n\nCornflour or potato starch,\n\nVegetable oil\n\nSauce\n\n1/2 cup dashi soup stock (konbu dashi)\n\n1/2 tbsp mirin\n\n1/2 tbsp light soy sauce\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Wrap tofu in paper towels and squeeze out excess water.\n\n2. Cut the tofu into 4 small squares.\n\n3. Coat the tofu cubes with cornflour evenly.\n\n4. Deep fry the tofu in pre-heated oil (170C, 340F) for about 4 minutes or until light golden brown.\n\n5. Drain the deep fried tofu on tempura papers and then place them on serving plates.\n\nIn a saucepan, bring the ingredients for the sauce to a boil. Pour the hot sauce over the tofu.\n\n6. Top each tofu with grated radish, bonito flakes and spring onions.",
  "cookTime": "PT10M",
  "recipeYield": "2",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "200g firm tofu,",
    "Grated white radish (daikon)",
    "Spring onions, chopped",
    "Bonito Flakes",
    "Cornflour or potato starch,",
    "Vegetable oil",
    "Sauce: 1/2 cup dashi soup stock (konbu dashi)",
    "Sauce: 1/2 tbsp mirin",
    "Sauce: 1/2 tbsp light soy sauce"
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "1. Wrap tofu in paper towels and squeeze out excess water."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "2. Cut the tofu into 4 small squares."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "3. Coat the tofu cubes with cornflour evenly."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "4. Deep fry the tofu in pre-heated oil (170C, 340F) for about 4 minutes or until light golden brown."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "5. Drain the deep fried tofu on tempura papers and then place them on serving plates."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "In a saucepan, bring the ingredients for the sauce to a boil. Pour the hot sauce over the tofu."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "6. Top each tofu with grated radish, bonito flakes and spring onions."
    }
